## Summary

The change rejects creating an owner when another owner already has the same last name **and** telephone, responding 409.

The escalation infrastructure already existed (`OwnerConflictException`, its handler responding `409 CONFLICT`, the escalation YAML, and the `EnsureOwnerUnique` step wired into `owners.POST.yml`). Only the matching rule needed adjusting.

**`EnsureOwnerUnique.java`** — narrowed the duplicate check from all-fields-identical (first name, last name, address, city, telephone) to **last name + telephone**:

```java
for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findByLastName(owner.getLastName())) {
    if (Objects.equals(existing.getLastName(), owner.getLastName())
            && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), owner.getTelephone())) {
        throw new OwnerConflictException(
                "An owner with the same last name and telephone already exists");
    }
}
```

`findByLastName` uses a prefix-`LIKE` query, so the exact `Objects.equals` on last name still guards correctly. Also updated the stale javadoc on `EnsureOwnerUnique` and `OwnerConflictException`.

